ppa: composite argb8888 images, and offer glyphs to the engine

The image path did not composite. It passed the source as the blend background
and the destination as a fully transparent foreground, spending the foreground
slot on a no-op to turn a blend into an opaque blit -- which is why
ppa_evaluate demanded an opaque RGB565/RGB888 image. Widening the format test
alone would have discarded the alpha, so the roles are swapped for a source
that carries one; opaque sources keep the blit.

Also fixes in_fg taking its picture dimensions from the source header while its
buffer was the destination (harmless only while that foreground stayed
transparent), drops a stray extern for a benchmark asset, and adds the glyph
draw unit in lv_draw_ppa_label.c -- a new file, created here by the diff.

Origin: b572be5 ("ppa: composite argb8888 images, and offer glyphs to the
engine").

